      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "For luxury brands, Quiet Luxury and high-concept indie folk carry the highest prestige due to their emphasis on understated elegance and artistic depth, effectively signaling socioeconomic status. Conversely, Drill music and urban-derived slang like \"no cap\" are best positioned as niche or street-level elements, functioning more as cultural signals within hip-hop subcultures rather than mainstream luxury indicators. While reggaeton dances and minimalist aesthetics can bridge some gaps depending on execution and execution, they generally lack the inherent \"sophistication\" reserved for high-end advertising narratives. Ultimately, brands aiming for an upscale image should prioritize the avant-garde, seeking to avoid trends perceived as disposable or overly populist.",
