      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Categorizing these terms relies heavily on the historical association between specific subcultures and mainstream elite values, often conflating \"urban roots\" with a lack of refinement rather than actual artistic merit. Luxury brands frequently seek to distance themselves from genres they view as commodified, celebrating hallmarks of wealth over the raw, street-level narratives where terms like \"glizzy\" originate. While indie folk and minimalist aesthetics intentionally cultivate an aura of exclusivity and quiet confidence, slang and music-producing duo that thrive on community-specific vernacular are often perceived by corporations as inherently \"unrefined\" due to this perceived class divide. This oversight, however, risks alienating sophisticated audiences who increasingly value authentic cultural immersion over traditional signals of status.",
